    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 acceptance tests passing).\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe optional, region-validated `postcode` field on owners, following the existing Spring/OpenAPI/MapStruct conventions in the repo:\n\n1. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (`type: string`, `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`), so it appears on both the create request DTO and the returned `Owner`. This drives the generated `@Pattern` that rejects a **malformed** postcode (e.g. `\"12\"`) with 400. I also attached a class-level `x-class-extra-annotation` (`@PostcodeValidation`) to `OwnerFields` for the cross-field range check.\n\n2. **Cross-field validation** \u2014 new `PostcodeValidation` annotation + `PostcodeValidator` (mirroring the existing `TelephoneValidation`/`TelephoneValidator` pattern). It validates **only when the postcode is present and well-formed**: it derives the region from the city (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) and enforces the range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099). An out-of-range postcode \u2192 400; a city with **no known region** accepts any 4-digit postcode; an **absent** postcode is always accepted (backward-compatible).\n\n3. **Persistence** \u2014 added the `postcode` field/column to the `Owner` entity and to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 used by the tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres). MapStruct maps it by name in both directions, so it's stored and returned. I also wired it into `updateOwner` to keep the editable-field set consistent.\n\nValidation errors flow through the existing `MethodArgumentNotValidException` handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, which returns 400.\n\nNote: I left the experimenter-owned acceptance test files untouched; the spec's out-of-range rejection is covered by the validator (e.g. Sydney + `\"3000\"` \u2192 400), even though the provided tests exercise only the store/absent/malformed cases.\n\nNo commit was made (this directory isn't a git repository, and you didn't ask me to).",
